    {
      "key": "edit",
      "name": "Edit a Still with Words",
      "description": "Change an image by describing the change. The model edits in place rather than regenerating, so composition and subject survive - the instruction should name what to alter and leave the rest unsaid.",
      "sourceId": "nodetool-base/Edit a Still with Words",
      "graph": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "id": "intro-comment",
            "type": "nodetool.workflows.base_node.Comment",
            "data": {
              "comment": "# Edit a Still with Words\n\nChanges an image by describing the change in words. The model edits the picture in place, so composition and subject stay as they were.\n\n**How it works:** \"Image\" supplies the picture. \"Instruction\" and the optional \"Directions\" are joined by \"Prompt\" into one text. \"Edit\" applies that text to the image at a strength of 0.6, and \"Result\" shows the edited still. Pick a model on \"Edit\" before running.\n\n**Try this:** Change \"Instruction\" to \"Replace the sky with heavy overcast\" and leave the rest of the scene unmentioned."
            },
            "ui_properties": {
              "position": {
                "x": 0,
                "y": 0
